00:48:28.838 --> 00:48:30.741 align:start size:78% position:22%
I'm gonna make
this sucker tough.

00:48:33.176 --> 00:48:35.545
Okay! We are done!

00:48:35.778 --> 00:48:37.380
Let's clean up.

00:48:37.413 --> 00:48:39.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wasn't that worth just,
the time we've put into it?

00:48:39.582 --> 00:48:41.919 align:start size:88% position:13%
CAROL: Yup.
CHIP: Good little sled.

00:48:43.152 --> 00:48:45.388 align:start size:84% position:16%
Okay, I'm gonna go
set this out there and

00:48:45.421 --> 00:48:47.824
try not to let Wade see
it so he doesn't want
to play with it yet.

00:48:48.458 --> 00:48:50.427
Making things is how we've
made a living, you know?

00:48:50.460 --> 00:48:53.596 align:start size:88% position:13%
Instead of buying sleds,
we've just been able to
obtain wood,

00:48:53.629 --> 00:48:55.098
put some work into
it and make sleds.

00:48:55.498 --> 00:48:57.567 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, if you really want to
have the best, you'll make it.

00:48:57.600 --> 00:48:59.202
If you want to have it
at all, you'll make it.

00:48:59.235 --> 00:49:03.941
If I want my grandson to
have it, I'll make it.

00:49:12.081 --> 00:49:14.985
GLENN: Whether it's a
human preying on them
or a pack of wolves,

00:49:16.219 --> 00:49:18.956
you're never going to find
a moose out here in this
country dying of old age.

00:49:19.989 --> 00:49:22.859
That's just all part
of the natural cycle.

00:49:28.097 --> 00:49:31.401
(bones cracking)

00:49:34.570 --> 00:49:36.206 line:0%
(groans)

00:49:36.539 --> 00:49:38.475 line:0%
There.

00:49:39.175 --> 00:49:41.111 line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Glenn
 has successfully
 harvested a moose,</i>

00:49:42.145 --> 00:49:44.715 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
<i> providing his family
 with a winter's worth
 of much-needed protein.</i>

00:49:46.916 --> 00:49:49.586
<i> With the meat processed, he
 now begins the back-breaking</i>

00:49:49.619 --> 00:49:53.423 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> task of transporting
 each large segment home
 before darkness falls.</i>

00:49:56.859 --> 00:49:58.762
GLENN: There! I got it!

00:49:59.262 --> 00:50:01.665
That's the last piece
I had to separate.

00:50:05.034 --> 00:50:07.604
Okay. I've got my
moose all cut up.

00:50:07.637 --> 00:50:11.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
Thankfully, Trisha,
Amelia, and Agatha
came over with a sled.

00:50:11.874 --> 00:50:15.045 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
One of the biggest
challenges of moose hunting is
just getting the animal home.

00:50:15.278 --> 00:50:17.781 line:0%
After I get it down,
I've got an awful lot
of weight to move.

00:50:22.852 --> 00:50:26.423
First moose I ever moved
out here, I carried the
entire thing on my back.

00:50:27.090 --> 00:50:31.895
Eleven loads, and my back was
in such bad shape after that

00:50:32.495 --> 00:50:34.431
I laid in bed for
about five days.

00:50:34.464 --> 00:50:36.132
Couldn't move.

00:50:36.165 --> 00:50:37.167
Then I got smart.

00:50:37.200 --> 00:50:38.835
I got a sled the next year.

00:50:38.868 --> 00:50:40.470
A simple thing,
a plastic sled.

00:50:40.503 --> 00:50:42.973
But it sure can help out.

00:50:44.207 --> 00:50:46.777
There's the canoe!

00:50:47.376 --> 00:50:49.112
So far, so good.

00:50:49.145 --> 00:50:51.448
But I got hundreds
and hundreds and
pounds here to move.

00:50:52.315 --> 00:50:55.652
I need to get it to where my
family can make use of it.

00:50:58.187 --> 00:51:00.524
(Bleep). Totally broke my sled.

00:51:04.794 --> 00:51:08.098
That neck is the heaviest,
most difficult piece of meat
for me to get in the canoe.

00:51:11.000 --> 00:51:14.104 align:start size:91% position:9%
Only way I was able to get
it in there was to drag
the whole sled in,

00:51:14.137 --> 00:51:16.139
and I broke the sled.

00:51:16.172 --> 00:51:17.707
Not very nice.

00:51:17.740 --> 00:51:20.911 align:start size:91% position:9%
Hopefully this is still
gonna be adequate to get
the rest of the meat down.

00:51:22.812 --> 00:51:25.615 align:start size:81% position:19%
But that's what
I got to deal with.

00:51:28.417 --> 00:51:31.387 align:start size:88% position:13%
This sled is necessary
for me to get this
moose out of the woods.

00:51:31.420 --> 00:51:34.558
Without it, I'm gonna
have a big problem.

00:51:35.925 --> 00:51:37.527
A sled's a basic
piece of equipment.

00:51:37.560 --> 00:51:40.063 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's right up there with my
rifle, my knife, and my canoe.

00:51:41.564 --> 00:51:44.201
Basic transportation.

00:51:45.301 --> 00:51:48.705 align:start size:84% position:16%
I got eight or nine
loads to go, hopefully
this thing holds up.

00:51:53.276 --> 00:51:58.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
There. Looks like my
sled's in three pieces now.

00:51:59.849 --> 00:52:02.385
But it's still helping a lot.

00:52:02.652 --> 00:52:05.422 align:start size:81% position:19%
Broken sled's
better than no sled.

00:52:06.622 --> 00:52:09.259 align:start size:97% position:3%
Really my biggest concern
at this point is just getting

00:52:09.292 --> 00:52:11.628 align:start size:88% position:13%
it back before any
big scavenger finds it.

00:52:11.894 --> 00:52:15.098 align:start size:91% position:9%
I mean there are
definitely bears around,
and wolves, or wolverines.

00:52:15.364 --> 00:52:18.868 align:start size:91% position:9%
If any of those animals
find this meat before I
get it all back into camp,

00:52:18.901 --> 00:52:20.670
they'll destroy it.

00:52:22.238 --> 00:52:25.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
What I've got to think about
is getting the job done before
anything else gets to it.

00:52:26.008 --> 00:52:27.777
This thing is falling apart.

00:52:33.616 --> 00:52:39.523 line:0%
♪ ♪

00:52:43.659 --> 00:52:45.595
GLENN: This thing
is falling apart.

00:52:51.067 --> 00:52:53.170
Sled came apart.

00:52:54.604 --> 00:52:57.107
Oh, boy.

00:52:58.374 --> 00:53:01.044
This sled's busted
right in half now.

00:53:01.077 --> 00:53:03.013
This is gonna be a problem.

00:53:03.779 --> 00:53:06.049
Sled broke, things happen,
you gotta find a solution.

00:53:08.351 --> 00:53:10.587
I got to make some kind of
emergency improvisation here.

00:53:12.321 --> 00:53:14.057
See what I can do.

00:53:17.860 --> 00:53:21.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
If I can just get
this the next 75 yards
down to the shore,

00:53:21.364 --> 00:53:22.865
I'll have a full canoe load.

00:53:22.898 --> 00:53:24.434
I can go home.

00:53:24.467 --> 00:53:26.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got another sled
there I can bring back over.

00:53:26.636 --> 00:53:29.072 align:start size:78% position:22%
Problem is
just getting this,
I can't lift it up

00:53:29.105 --> 00:53:31.875
and carry it across
this tussocky ground
down to that beach.

00:53:32.108 --> 00:53:33.643
No way.

00:53:33.676 --> 00:53:35.745
But I might be able
to do something here.

00:53:36.746 --> 00:53:39.583
This is the biggest piece.

00:53:41.717 --> 00:53:44.621
Put a hole in there.

00:53:46.055 --> 00:53:51.228 align:start size:88% position:13%
If I just shingle
it like this, I'm taking
the two biggest pieces,

00:53:51.794 --> 00:53:54.331
overlap them, try to
latch it back together.

00:53:54.864 --> 00:53:56.966
Put the heaviest part of the
meat right here in the front,

00:53:56.999 --> 00:53:58.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
have the hoof
dragging out the back.

00:53:58.701 --> 00:54:01.404 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think I might be able to
make it to the beach that way.

00:54:04.507 --> 00:54:07.911
A lot of times I've been
in difficult situations and
not had much to work with.

00:54:10.413 --> 00:54:14.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if you stop, think
about it, and use your head,
you can find a solution.

00:54:20.222 --> 00:54:22.859
Hey, it's sliding.

00:54:26.062 --> 00:54:28.965
It's a funny thing, I've
been doing this for years.

00:54:28.998 --> 00:54:31.634
And every year,
it's difficult.

00:54:31.667 --> 00:54:35.938 align:start size:91% position:9%
You have to wonder, like,
why am I making getting
food so complicated?

00:54:35.971 --> 00:54:40.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
But after it's all done and
you're sitting down there,
eating that tenderloin.

00:54:41.777 --> 00:54:44.080
You forget all this
pain and suffering.

00:54:44.113 --> 00:54:46.082
It all goes away so fast.

00:54:46.115 --> 00:54:51.754
When you bite into that first
juicy steak, there's nothing
that tastes the same as meat

00:54:51.787 --> 00:54:55.425 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you hunted yourself
and put the effort
into getting back home

00:54:55.458 --> 00:54:57.761
and putting on the table.

00:54:59.729 --> 00:55:02.332
There. Okay.

00:55:07.036 --> 00:55:09.339
You get attached to
your tools out here.

00:55:09.372 --> 00:55:12.008 align:start size:84% position:16%
I get attached to my
tools because I depend
on them so much.

00:55:12.441 --> 00:55:14.844
This sled right here,
I've had it for years.

00:55:14.944 --> 00:55:18.915
I've moved literally
thousands of pounds of
meat with this sled,

00:55:19.248 --> 00:55:22.218 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that's the last
load of meat this sled's
ever going to move.

00:55:22.885 --> 00:55:26.056
We shared some pretty
good times together.

00:55:28.991 --> 00:55:30.993
I've been working 18 hours.

00:55:31.026 --> 00:55:33.796
I got to grab a bite to eat
in camp, get a little rest,

00:55:33.829 --> 00:55:36.700 align:start size:88% position:13%
and get back as soon as
I can before anything
gets that meat.

00:55:38.601 --> 00:55:42.706
I've always operated
alone, so I'm used
to taking that risk.

00:55:49.278 --> 00:55:53.816 align:start size:97% position:3%
JESSIE: I enjoy the
uncertainty that winter brings
and I enjoy just stepping up

00:55:53.849 --> 00:55:56.820
to the challenge of
whatever it brings.

00:56:10.266 --> 00:56:14.003 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Getting my dog food, uh,
cooker loaded up with some
wood before I head out to go

00:56:14.303 --> 00:56:16.539 line:0%
check my traps and see if
I got any action out there.

00:56:17.873 --> 00:56:19.675
Set some traps a
couple of days ago.

00:56:19.708 --> 00:56:22.245 align:start size:91% position:9%
So, hopefully I got
something in those traps.

00:56:23.446 --> 00:56:27.150 line:0%
The temperature has dropped,
so definitely gonna probably
be seeing a lot of changes out

00:56:27.183 --> 00:56:28.885 line:0%
there and a lot more ice.

00:56:28.918 --> 00:56:31.988 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Uh, definitely feels like
winter has finally got here.

00:56:32.955 --> 00:56:37.093 align:start size:97% position:3%
Get this fire going here
and, uh, that way my dog food
will be cooked this evening

00:56:37.126 --> 00:56:40.964
whenever I get home and,
uh, it's kind of the start
to every day around here.

00:56:41.664 --> 00:56:45.268 align:start size:97% position:3%
Get a good routine going,
and then you can, uh, be able
to afford some time to go out

00:56:45.301 --> 00:56:47.470 align:start size:91% position:9%
and hopefully
get some beaver right now.

00:57:00.249 --> 00:57:03.519
It's a good time of year to
be able to be out watching
what these beaver are doing.

00:57:03.552 --> 00:57:06.589
If you don't get out and
look around, you just don't
know what's out there.

00:57:07.790 --> 00:57:11.194
Opportunity is all over out
here you just got to get
out and go out and find it.

00:57:11.727 --> 00:57:14.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, when I go out there
in the woods, opportunity
tends to cross my path

00:57:15.231 --> 00:57:18.168
and I'm the type of person
that takes advantage of that.

00:57:20.870 --> 00:57:23.039
I see some movement up there.

00:57:25.107 --> 00:57:27.109
Looks like a grouse.

00:57:27.142 --> 00:57:30.647 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm gonna try to take
a shot at it with my .22 here.

00:57:34.250 --> 00:57:35.552
(gunshot)

00:57:40.956 --> 00:57:43.092 align:start size:88% position:13%
Got it! All right, man!
Awesome!

00:57:43.459 --> 00:57:45.562 align:start size:88% position:13%
I haven't seen many
grouse around this year.

00:57:45.794 --> 00:57:49.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come out here to go check
my beaver traps, brought my
gun with me, found a grouse.

00:57:50.499 --> 00:57:53.436
With the snow being
on the ground, and
this bird being dark,

00:57:53.469 --> 00:57:54.871
it stuck right out
to me, you know.

00:57:54.904 --> 00:57:57.306 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I was able to see
it out of the corner
of my eye moving.

00:57:57.339 --> 00:58:00.376
Just like I was the other
day, using my surroundings
to my advantage with, uh,

00:58:00.409 --> 00:58:04.047
hunting the rabbits because
they're white on dark ground,
this is the reverse of that.

00:58:04.947 --> 00:58:06.415
Clean, organic
meat right here.

00:58:06.448 --> 00:58:07.716
This is the best.

00:58:07.750 --> 00:58:09.719 align:start size:84% position:16%
This is just a bonus
for going out here to
check my traps.

00:58:10.286 --> 00:58:11.654
This is gonna be delicious.

00:58:11.687 --> 00:58:14.524 align:start size:81% position:19%
Gonna eat this
first thing tonight.

00:58:16.258 --> 00:58:19.562
One of the things that I love
about living out here is you
just get out in the backyard

00:58:19.595 --> 00:58:22.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you start putting in
some effort and you can come
away with something to eat,

00:58:22.798 --> 00:58:24.534 align:start size:81% position:19%
and that's a very
pleasurable feeling.

00:58:24.567 --> 00:58:26.569
It's a valuable
use of my time.

00:58:26.602 --> 00:58:28.604 align:start size:84% position:16%
I love to just go
out and walk and hunt.

00:58:28.637 --> 00:58:31.541
Opportunity presents itself,
come away with a bird to eat.

00:58:34.009 --> 00:58:37.346 align:start size:84% position:16%
Getting closer over
here to my first trap.

00:58:37.379 --> 00:58:41.317
Hoping to get at least one
beaver would be real nice.

00:58:41.550 --> 00:58:44.153 align:start size:81% position:19%
Trap number one,
the moment of truth.

00:58:45.854 --> 00:58:47.790
No, nothing in there.

00:58:47.823 --> 00:58:49.325 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're gonna go
check the other ones.

00:58:49.358 --> 00:58:51.327
Definitely froze up overnight.

00:58:51.360 --> 00:58:53.630 align:start size:88% position:13%
Hopefully those beavers
came out for one
last snack on the bank.

00:58:54.229 --> 00:58:56.399
Before this ice froze up.

00:58:56.432 --> 00:58:58.968
Yup, nothing in
these traps here.

00:58:59.702 --> 00:59:02.572 align:start size:81% position:19%
This is trap two and
trap number three,
nothing in there.

00:59:03.272 --> 00:59:05.241 align:start size:81% position:19%
Still got one
more trap to check.

00:59:05.274 --> 00:59:07.243 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm going over to
check my fourth trap.

00:59:07.276 --> 00:59:08.844
It's not like the
other three traps.

00:59:08.878 --> 00:59:12.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
I put this one under
the water so it's under the
ice so there's a way bigger

00:59:12.314 --> 00:59:14.984
chance that I'm gonna have
a beaver in this set than

00:59:15.017 --> 00:59:16.485 align:start size:81% position:19%
these other sets
cause these beavers,

00:59:16.518 --> 00:59:19.855 align:start size:84% position:16%
they can't come out
up on the bank anymore
with this ice, so.

00:59:19.888 --> 00:59:22.659 align:start size:84% position:16%
Oh, wow. There's
definitely some broken
up ice over here.

00:59:24.326 --> 00:59:26.696 align:start size:84% position:16%
I might have
something in this one.

00:59:26.962 --> 00:59:28.998
My trap is under
the ice right here.

00:59:29.565 --> 00:59:31.434
I can't really see
underneath this.

00:59:31.467 --> 00:59:33.169
It's frozen pretty thick.

00:59:36.071 --> 00:59:37.273
There's the trap.

00:59:41.176 --> 00:59:43.012 align:start position:0% line:0%
JESSIE: This is
definitely my highest hopes for

00:59:43.045 --> 00:59:44.881 line:0%
having something in
this trap right here.

00:59:46.015 --> 00:59:48.084
There's the trap and
there's nothing in it.

00:59:50.185 --> 00:59:52.755 align:start size:91% position:9%
I thought we had warm
enough weather that this
ice wasn't gonna develop.

00:59:53.355 --> 00:59:55.625
This ice right here prevents
the beavers from coming up

00:59:55.658 --> 00:59:57.493
into my traps that
are on the bank.

00:59:57.526 --> 01:00:00.096 align:start size:88% position:13%
About in one more week,
I'll be able to walk
out on this ice

01:00:00.129 --> 01:00:02.732
and I can set some traps
underneath it that I know
are gonna be productive.

01:00:03.699 --> 01:00:05.568 align:start size:91% position:9%
I know I'm gonna get these
beavers at some point.

01:00:05.601 --> 01:00:07.837 align:start size:88% position:13%
I come out here and
I found a good location.

01:00:08.370 --> 01:00:10.807 align:start size:91% position:9%
That's a good thing to
have in my back pocket and
know that it's out here.

01:00:13.008 --> 01:00:15.912 align:start size:97% position:3%
With the way the conditions
are right now there's no point
in leaving these traps here.

01:00:16.445 --> 01:00:19.415 align:start size:91% position:9%
These traps aren't
going to do any good here
so I'm gonna spring them,

01:00:19.448 --> 01:00:21.084
take them home.

01:00:25.954 --> 01:00:27.390
Didn't come away
with any beaver,

01:00:27.423 --> 01:00:29.091 align:start size:84% position:16%
but as soon as
that ice thickens up,

01:00:29.124 --> 01:00:31.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll be able to go out
there and reset those traps.

01:00:31.393 --> 01:00:33.529
Right now I got, you know,
some nice rabbits to cook up

01:00:33.562 --> 01:00:35.665 align:start size:91% position:9%
and a nice grouse
I'd picked up on the way.

01:00:36.198 --> 01:00:38.034
And I'm about to
have myself a meal.

01:00:38.367 --> 01:00:40.670
Looking forward to going
home and having a nice fire

01:00:40.703 --> 01:00:43.106 align:start size:88% position:13%
and cooking up
some of this fresh meat.

01:00:50.546 --> 01:00:53.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is one rabbit and
this grouse here will be a
couple days' worth of food.

01:00:55.050 --> 01:00:57.453
Putting in the effort,
come out with the reward.

01:00:58.587 --> 01:01:02.792
Now, I get to enjoy the
reward here and, uh, eat
myself some fresh rabbit.

01:01:08.363 --> 01:01:11.434 align:start size:78% position:22%
Hmm. That's good,
real good.

01:01:12.134 --> 01:01:14.537 align:start size:84% position:16%
My grandpa really
liked hunting rabbits.

01:01:14.570 --> 01:01:15.905
I feel like if he was here,

01:01:15.938 --> 01:01:19.375 align:start size:88% position:13%
he'd be real proud of
the way I'm living and
that makes me feel good.

01:01:21.043 --> 01:01:23.079 align:start size:97% position:3%
This is a real
transition time of year here.

01:01:23.112 --> 01:01:24.680 align:start size:78% position:22%
It's gonna be
winter real soon.

01:01:24.713 --> 01:01:28.084 align:start size:88% position:13%
You really just gotta
adapt to living by the
cycles of the land here,

01:01:28.117 --> 01:01:29.652
you know, and the seasons.

01:01:29.685 --> 01:01:32.955
And the, know where the
animals are, and know
when you can get them.

01:01:33.322 --> 01:01:37.226
One of my biggest beliefs out
here that's really helped me
with everything is to devote

01:01:37.259 --> 01:01:40.063
yourself to the perfection
of whatever it is you pursue.

01:01:41.063 --> 01:01:45.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
To pursue everything
with hard work, dignity,
integrity, and persistence.

01:01:48.504 --> 01:01:51.407
Maybe sometimes I'll have
a little luck but that luck
is a residue of design.

01:01:52.674 --> 01:01:54.643
Every time I go out there,
things are gonna happen.

01:01:54.676 --> 01:01:56.579 align:start size:91% position:9%
But I got to go out
there to make them happen.

01:01:56.612 --> 01:01:58.881
And I enjoy that
kind of lifestyle.

01:01:59.615 --> 01:02:02.952 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's a lifestyle
that always keeps you on your
toes, always keeps you moving.

01:02:03.152 --> 01:02:05.721 align:start size:88% position:13%
I had my trials
and my tribulations
but I kept coming at it

01:02:05.754 --> 01:02:07.657
and kept coming at
it and here I am now.

01:02:08.323 --> 01:02:11.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Learning every year how
to thrive and survive more.

01:02:17.366 --> 01:02:20.002
GLENN: Many years ago, I had a
vision of what I wanted to do.

01:02:20.035 --> 01:02:21.971
To live off the land.

01:02:22.237 --> 01:02:24.507 align:start size:88% position:13%
Hunt for my food,
live in the wilderness.

01:02:25.941 --> 01:02:28.444 align:start size:81% position:19%
And the Brooks
Range is the place.

01:02:45.861 --> 01:02:48.498 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
This weighs
about 100 pounds.

01:02:48.831 --> 01:02:50.233
Pretty big head.

01:02:52.068 --> 01:02:55.638 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> NARRATOR: After hunting a
 bull moose, Glenn places the
 final piece on his meat rack,</i>

01:02:56.338 --> 01:02:59.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> culminating in a</i> <i> winter's
 worth of protein for
 himself and his family.</i>

01:03:03.679 --> 01:03:06.249 align:start size:84% position:16%
GLENN: There!
Got the meat hung up.

01:03:07.282 --> 01:03:08.984
Air can circulate around it.

01:03:09.017 --> 01:03:11.387 align:start size:91% position:9%
This is good, it's already
getting a dry crust.

01:03:11.420 --> 01:03:13.589
And that's the key
to preserving meat.

01:03:15.591 --> 01:03:17.893
So this meat's gonna be okay.

01:03:17.926 --> 01:03:19.628
That meat's not gonna spoil.

01:03:19.661 --> 01:03:23.465
As long as it's kept dry and
clean, hanging there with good
air circulation around it,

01:03:23.498 --> 01:03:25.201 align:start size:84% position:16%
it'll be just
fine until it freezes.

01:03:26.802 --> 01:03:28.871
Nice chunk of fat right there.

01:03:30.339 --> 01:03:32.007
What an awesome hunt!

01:03:32.040 --> 01:03:34.610
Walking around this lake,
looking for this moose.

01:03:34.643 --> 01:03:36.646 align:start size:78% position:22%
Unbelievable,
gorgeous country.

01:03:38.213 --> 01:03:39.615
I sure got my exercise.

01:03:39.648 --> 01:03:41.717
It was a lot of work,
but this is the payoff.

01:03:51.693 --> 01:03:53.963
AMELIA: Agatha, you're gonna
eat a tongue and tenderloin.

01:03:54.263 --> 01:03:56.098 align:start size:88% position:13%
GLENN: All right.
Let's have some dinner.

01:03:56.131 --> 01:03:59.836 align:start size:97% position:3%
TRISHA: Yum.
GLENN: Yeah, it's finger food.

01:04:00.869 --> 01:04:02.738 align:start size:91% position:9%
TRISHA: It's finger food.
GLENN: Moose tongue!

01:04:03.105 --> 01:04:05.675 align:start size:97% position:3%
AMELIA: (Inaudible) of course.
TRISHA: Oh, lucky you.

01:04:07.576 --> 01:04:10.346 align:start size:91% position:9%
GLENN: Hmm. Moose tongue,
it's been a year!

01:04:12.714 --> 01:04:14.951 align:start size:84% position:16%
Makes me think of
the first time I ever
got a moose out here.

01:04:15.717 --> 01:04:19.655 align:start size:81% position:19%
And, uh, I put so
much energy into it.

01:04:21.189 --> 01:04:24.660
Hunted for about two weeks,
got a moose and I was just
sitting here enjoying all the

01:04:24.693 --> 01:04:26.863 align:start size:88% position:13%
different tasty tidbits
for the first time.

01:04:28.363 --> 01:04:30.032
But I was all by myself.

01:04:30.065 --> 01:04:32.268
Didn't have anybody
to share it with.

01:04:32.301 --> 01:04:35.071
This is so much nicer,
having you all here.

01:04:35.837 --> 01:04:37.806 align:start size:75% position:25%
TRISHA: More?
Oh, my goodness.

01:04:37.839 --> 01:04:39.041
GLENN: Oh, she's
totally into it!

01:04:39.074 --> 01:04:40.209
More, more, more.

01:04:40.242 --> 01:04:42.011 align:start size:78% position:22%
TRISHA: Show Mommy
what you want.

01:04:42.044 --> 01:04:43.746 align:start size:78% position:22%
GLENN: Isn't that
good, Agatha?

01:04:44.046 --> 01:04:46.148
Yeah? Moose tongue!

01:04:49.785 --> 01:04:52.321
It took a while to get
it all together, but you
know this was my dream.

01:04:53.555 --> 01:04:57.159
It's what I always wanted
to do, live out in the
wilderness with my family.

01:04:57.759 --> 01:05:01.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of my basic philosophies
in life, know yourself,
know what makes you happy,

01:05:01.563 --> 01:05:03.132
and then pursue it.

01:05:04.166 --> 01:05:06.035
And that's what I did here.

01:05:06.068 --> 01:05:07.436
I wanted to live
in the wilderness.

01:05:07.469 --> 01:05:09.271
I wanted to have
a family out here.

01:05:09.304 --> 01:05:11.374
And I have it.

01:05:11.940 --> 01:05:15.344
I have everything that
really matters to me.

01:05:19.915 --> 01:05:23.686
SUE: No matter where you are,
home can be the coolest place
on the planet of the Earth.

01:05:24.186 --> 01:05:27.390
But it's good to get outside
and get a stretch of the legs.

01:05:39.101 --> 01:05:40.736 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
I've got my
ptarmigan in there.

01:05:40.769 --> 01:05:44.340 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
The oil, that's actually
bear fat that's rendered down.

01:05:44.373 --> 01:05:48.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some spices, I'm adding
some spinach from my garden.

01:05:48.443 --> 01:05:50.613
I take it and I freeze it.

01:05:50.846 --> 01:05:53.349
These are some mushrooms
I got earlier in the year.

01:05:56.151 --> 01:05:57.787
It was a good day.

01:06:00.122 --> 01:06:04.060 align:start size:91% position:9%
Did I fail at killing the
bear, taking, harvesting
